<p>When hail, wind, fire, or water damages a Dallas home or business, the repair has to meet the building codes in force today, not the codes that applied when the building went up. That is true for a 1920s Craftsman in the M Streets, a 1960s ranch in Lake Highlands, and a 2010s office building off the Tollway alike. The gap between how a building was built and how it must be rebuilt is one of the most common sources of confusion on insurance claims. This page summarizes Dallas building codes and how they relate to insurance repairs, using information published by the City of Dallas Development Services Department on dallascityhall.com.</p>
